      "female",
      "male"
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "Single front-view line drawing used as reference; the torso leans toward the ankle because the rig's arm reach cannot brace behind while holding the ankle, and the hand lands on the lower shin rather than the ankle bone.",
      "Buttocks, right heel and left sole share floor contact; root height is the female/male mean within the 10 mm floor tolerance.",
      "Authored on rig/female.glb; the male reuses the same rotations with the hips-height-relative root offset."
    ],
